From: Stephen Kent <43362477+kentstephen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 20:22:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] wasm32-emscripten support and ranges= chunk pruning for
 read_zarr

- Gate zarrs_http off wasm; route all stores through DuckDbStore on wasm
- Single-thread rayon global pool at extension init on wasm
- CFLAGS -fPIC for zstd-sys on wasm32-unknown-emscripten
- DuckDbStore::get_partial_many loops on short reads (duckdb-wasm HTTP FS
  returns 16 KiB pieces)
- Add ranges=['dim:lo:hi', ...] named param to read_zarr: prunes chunks on
  coordinate min/max at bind (parse_dim_range, build_work_units_pruned).
  Kept chunks still emit all rows, so bounds must be repeated in WHERE.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015DQGNDQN7rRXCfEQ7wL4cr
